body:
GA,

Marcus caught a UX bug during live testing. On Question 12 (graph + vertex inputs), he entered the correct vertex (3, -6) but the entire question showed feedback_wrong in red because 2 of 5 graph points were off. The red message said "Vertex is (h,k) from a(x-h)^2 + k. Here h=3, k=-6" — which made it look like his vertex entry was wrong, when actually it was correct.

ROOT CAUSE
gradeExam() uses a single qCorrect boolean for the entire question. If graph fails, qCorrect=false and the question-level feedback_wrong fires regardless of whether vertex inputs were right. There is no per-input visual feedback.

THE FIX
After grading each number input in gradeExam(), apply a visual indicator to the input field itself:
  - Correct input: green left border
  - Wrong or empty input: red left border

Implementation in gradeExam(), inside the numberInputs.forEach loop (currently around line 765):

  // After the existing tolerance check, add visual feedback:
  numberInputs.forEach(function(n) {
      var isCorrect = !isNaN(n.val) && Math.abs(n.val - n.answer) <= n.tolerance;
      if (!isCorrect) qCorrect = false;
      // Visual feedback on the input element
      if (n.el) {
          n.el.style.borderColor = isCorrect ? 'var(--color-correct)' : 'var(--color-incorrect)';
          n.el.style.borderWidth = '2px';
      }
  });

You will need to store the element reference alongside val/answer/tolerance. Update the push:
  numberInputs.push({ el: el2, val: val, answer: inp.answer, tolerance: inp.tolerance || 0.01 });

Also update the question-level feedback for graph questions when vertex inputs are correct but graph is wrong. Change the feedback_wrong message logic: if qCorrect is false ONLY because of the graph (all numberInputs passed), show a graph-specific message instead of the generic feedback_wrong:

  var allInputsCorrect = numberInputs.every(function(n) {
      return !isNaN(n.val) && Math.abs(n.val - n.answer) <= n.tolerance;
  });
  if (q.graph && !gd.gradeResult && allInputsCorrect) {
      msg = 'Graph points need work — but your vertex is correct. Check the plotted points.';
  }

SCOPE: exam.html only. No data file changes.

DEFINITION OF DONE
1. Each number input gets green/red border after grading
2. When graph fails but vertex inputs are correct, message says vertex is right
3. Adversary test: verify a question where graph fails but inputs are correct shows green inputs + graph-specific message
4. Commit: fix(GA): per-input visual grading feedback, graph+vertex message split

— FA
